        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "790a95fa-3491-5f2e-90d4-9d6e8595bce0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Carmelo Anthony, Chauncey Billups, Anthony Carter, Renaldo Balkman, Shelden Williams, Corey Brewer, Wilson Chandler, Danilo Gallinari, Raymond Felton, Timofey Mozgov, Kosta Koufos\n- Organizations: Denver Nuggets, New York Knicks, Minnesota Timberwolves, Golden State Warriors\n- Events: 2005 NBA draft, 2011 three-team NBA trade\n- Topics: NBA player transactions, draft picks\n\nFacts:\n- Raymond Felton was drafted fifth overall in the 2005 NBA draft.\n- On February 21, 2011, the Denver Nuggets traded Carmelo Anthony to the New York Knicks in a three-team trade involving the Minnesota Timberwolves after months of rumors and speculation.\n- In the February 21, 2011 trade, the Denver Nuggets sent Chauncey Billups, Anthony Carter, Renaldo Balkman, Shelden Williams, and Corey Brewer to the New York Knicks.\n- In the February 21, 2011 trade, the Denver Nuggets received Wilson Chandler, Danilo Gallinari, Raymond Felton, Timofey Mozgov, Kosta Koufos, New York's 2014 first-round draft pick, and Golden State's 2012 and 2013 second-round draft picks.\n- Over his NBA career, Raymond Felton played for the Charlotte Bobcats, New York Knicks, Denver Nuggets, Portland Trail Blazers, Dallas Mavericks, and Los Angeles Clippers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "69a1584c-a42f-5d9b-b9cc-65bb551ee60e",
        "text": "Page: 2010–11 Denver Nuggets season. Sentence: After half a season of rumors and speculation, the Nuggets granted Carmelo Anthony his wish by trading him to the New York Knicks on February 21 as part of a three-team trade with the Minnesota Timberwolves.\nPage: 2010–11 Denver Nuggets season. Sentence: The blockbuster trade also sent Chauncey Billups, Anthony Carter, Renaldo Balkman, Shelden Williams and Corey Brewer to the Knicks for Wilson Chandler, Danilo Gallinari, Raymond Felton, Timofey Mozgov, Kosta Koufos, New York's first round pick in the 2014 draft and Golden State's second round picks in 2012 and 2013.\nPage: Raymond Felton. Sentence: Felton was drafted fifth overall in the 2005 NBA draft.\nPage: Raymond Felton. Sentence: Over his career, Felton has been a member of the Charlotte Bobcats, New York Knicks (twice), Denver Nuggets, Portland Trail Blazers, Dallas Mavericks and Los Angeles Clippers.",
